- A plain block comment at the top is the header comment when there is no `//!` comment.
- Signatures print as written on one line, with generics, a const's or static's type, and a type alias's type.
== args
input/block-comment.rs
== file input/block-comment.rs
/* This is a block comment */

fn main() {}
== stdout
input/block-comment.rs (3 lines)
This is a block comment
[L3-L3] fn main()
